# SPDX-License-Identifier: AGPL-3.0-only
#
# The reader on Curse of the Azure Bonds (#588): the log, an entry's
# pages forward and back, its picture, the log again, and the screen
# given back whole. `tests/sessions/curse-notes.rec` is the same walk
# as hashes; this is the same claim in pixels and in what the screen
# says, on `docs/playable-curse.md` leg 2's keys.
# A single leg, for rdr-page.leg's reason: the log and a page cover the
# screen, so a rect that allowed them would check nothing, and `N`
# reaches the program in a seam-off run.
# On this program a screen the seam draws is settled within a dump of
# its key at `--speed 386`, where Pool of Radiance's takes about 230
# frames at its own; each range below starts one dump after the key.
# Driven on the Steam copy with its shipped slots (`curse-slots`).

about the reader on Curse: the log, an entry's pages and picture, and the screen given back exactly
kind single
program START.EXE
speed 386
store tests/visual/curse-reader-store.txt
seam journal
until 153122200
every 25

# The challenge, which takes any letter, slot A, the opening event's two
# screens and the innkeeper's, whose second cites entry 31.
key P@2500
key A@2650
key Return@2800
key L@2950
key A@3100
key B@3250
key Return@3550
key Return@3850
key Left@4000
key Left@4600
key Up@4750
key Return@4900
key Return@5050

# `Notes` opens the log and Return the row the cursor is on. `NEXT` to
# the second page, Backspace back, `NEXT` twice onto the picture, and
# out by `EXIT` twice: to the log, and to the adventuring screen.
key N@5350
key Return@5500
key N@5800
key Backspace@6100
key N@6400
key N@6700
key E@7000
key E@7300

# The party's bar with `Notes` on it, before the log is opened.
same 5100-5350

# The log, page 1, page 2, page 1 again, page 2 again, the picture and
# the log again: each holding still with nothing pressed.
same 5375-5500
same 5525-5800
same 5825-6100
same 6125-6400
same 6425-6700
same 6725-7000
same 7025-7300

# Backspace steps back to the page `NEXT` left, and `NEXT` forward to
# the one it left: the same screens, not merely settled ones.
equal 5525 6125
equal 5825 6425

